title: Profile and optimize memory usage during map diffing (target <1 GB for super large maps)
updated_at: "2026-09-11T04:14:35Z"
---
Profile memory usage when diffing large maps and optimize so peak RSS stays under 1 GB even for super large maps. Likely needs light memory management: avoid keeping references to old objects alive (event handlers, caches, captured locals) so GC can reclaim between phases, and stream/release intermediate buffers instead of accumulating them. Test map pair: 'Sweet 2 burger v206 -> v207' in ~/Downloads/. Acceptance: measured peak memory for that pair (and a stress case) documented before/after; no functional regressions in diff output.

Lane plan: B065 and B066 both touch the diff path (DiffMode/MapContentComparison/DiffData), so they run as ONE serial lane in a single worktree. Order: B066 first (small, changes modified-detection semantics), then B065 (memory profiling/optimization measured against the corrected diff). Sequenced 2026-09-11.